# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/stream-1 window (prompt lookup on the production path; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/stream-1 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stream-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-stream-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): the Swift checkpoint production serves, from its own converted-weight directory (the weight cache must be found, as in the s5 window).
# TL3 (the CANDIDATE of the lone-user pair): TL2 with the 'lookup' arm. A lone user is where idle segments are free (a two-candidate verify would live here, docs/tp4-tree-verify.md), so this pair is the one that
# says what the lookup alone does for the fast lane: its 'speed' line (decode tok/s of one stream, control against lookup) and its tau. READ as TL1. Duration (estimate): 45 min.
# ADD before pushing: C2_TAULAB_PAIR_CONTROL=<the digits of the workflow run id of TL2> (the job reader refuses a candidate arm without it, so no verdict would be produced).
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset taulab
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-stream-1
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_TAULAB_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-fx-traffic-s5
C2_TAULAB_DRAFTER_ARM=lookup
C2_TAULAB_ARMS=A2
C2_TAULAB_DEADLINE=35
C2_TAULAB_IN_FLIGHT=1
